  "title": "Vertex AI v1beta1: Breaking Changes, Egress Control & Gen AI Continuation",
  "summary": "Vertex AI's v1beta1 API introduces breaking changes to agent and candidate properties, along with a type change for file citation metadata. New features include network egress control for agents, continuation tokens for long content generation, and enhanced observability filtering.",
  "details": "This update includes several breaking changes: the `effectiveIdentity` property in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Agent` and the `continuationToken` property in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Candidate` are now read-only. If your code was setting these fields, it will now break. Additionally, the `customMetadata` field in `GenaiVertexV1beta1FileCitation` has changed its type from a reference to `GenaiVertexV1beta1Struct` to a generic `object` with `additionalProperties` of `any`. Developers should update their client code to reflect these changes.\n\nOn the feature front, `CloudAiLargeModelsVisionGenerateVideoExperimentsSuperResConfig` now includes a `tileSmoothing` boolean property for smoother video upscaling. Agent configurations gain more control over network egress with the new `mode` field in `GenaiVertexV1beta1EnvironmentConfigEgressRule`, including a `DISABLED` option. Long-running content generation can now be resumed using new `continuationToken` fields in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerateContentRequest`, `GenaiVertexV1beta1Interaction`, and `GenaiVertexV1beta1InteractionStatusUpdate`. The `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Candidate.finishReason` enum now includes `CONTINUATION` and `MALFORMED_RESPONSE` to support this. `GenaiVertexV1beta1InteractionStatusUpdate` also gains `usage` statistics. For enhanced security, `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentAnomalyDetectionScope` now supports `encryptionSpec` for customer-managed encryption keys (CMEK). Observability filtering is improved with the new `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1OnlineEvaluatorCloudObservabilityStringPredicate` for `serviceVersion` in session and trace scopes. Finally, `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SchemaPromptSpecStructuredPrompt` can now include `contentMetadata` with `citationMetadata` and `groundingMetadata` for richer context on generated content.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
